# MS/TP frames (Clause 9.3): preamble 55 ff, type, destination, source,
# length, header CRC, then data and its CRC. The first two are the worked
# examples of Annex G: header CRC 8c, and data CRC 10 bd sent low octet first.

55 ff 00 10 05 00 00 8c => token to 16 from 5
55 ff 06 10 05 00 03 9c 01 22 30 10 bd => data-not-expecting-reply to 16 from 5 data 012230
# Finding a successor, and the answer.
55 ff 01 06 05 00 00 b1 => poll-for-master to 6 from 5
55 ff 02 05 06 00 00 0b => reply-to-poll-for-master to 5 from 6
# A ReadProperty request for analog-input 1, present-value, and the token after it.
55 ff 05 06 05 00 0d 55 01 04 00 05 01 0c 0c 00 00 00 01 19 55 f3 89 => data-expecting-reply to 6 from 5 data 01040005010c0c000000011955
55 ff 07 05 06 00 00 93 => reply-postponed to 5 from 6
55 ff 06 ff 05 00 08 e3 01 20 ff ff 00 ff 10 08 15 b6 => data-not-expecting-reply to 255 from 5 data 0120ffff00ff1008
55 ff 03 06 05 00 02 41 7a 7a 2e de => test-request to 6 from 5 data 7a7a
55 ff 04 05 06 00 02 e5 7a 7a 2e de => test-response to 5 from 6 data 7a7a
# Annex T: an extended frame, COBS-encoded and masked with 55 so no octet is
# zero, with a CRC-32K; its length field is two short so old stations skip it.
55 ff 21 06 05 00 0a 47 57 54 54 57 45 57 5d 50 3e dd 87 60 => extended-not-expecting-reply to 6 from 5 data 010000100008
55 ff 20 06 05 00 0f c2 59 54 57 56 51 50 53 52 5d 5c 5f 5e 50 72 ee b1 e8 => extended-expecting-reply to 6 from 5 data 0102030405060708090a0b
